What's happening with climate and nature, and what does it mean for everyday life in the UK?

Join us for a screening of the **People's Emergency Briefing** - an eye-opening 50-minute film bringing together nine leading UK scientists and experts with the latest evidence and why it matters for:

- Extreme weather
- Food security
- Health
- Cost of living

The film is based on the National Emergency Briefing in Westminster, with appearances from Chris Packham, Deborah Meaden, Jennifer Saunders and voices from across the UK. It will be introduced by George Monbiot, and afterwards there'll be an **open discussion** about what it means for our community and what we can do locally.

Local resident **Simon Oldridge**, who co-founded the National Emergency Briefing, will be joining us. Around 6,000 screenings have now taken place in halls, community centres and workplaces across the country - don't miss the chance to see it in the place it all started.

**Seats are free but limited, so please book in advance.** If you book and then can't make it, please let the organisers know so your ticket can go to someone else. Bring a friend, neighbour, colleague or family member - everyone is welcome.

---

- **Doors open 6.30pm** for a 7pm start
- **Refreshments** from Things Happen Here and Pizzalogica
- Co-organised by Dartington Parish Council, Dartington Parochial Church Council, the Dartington Recreation Association and the Leadership and Resilience Centre

Learn more about the briefing at [nebriefing.org](https://www.nebriefing.org), and see [thingshappenhere.co.uk](https://thingshappenhere.co.uk/) for venue details.
